#X obj 60 678 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Inlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 706 1 float: note number. Velocity is taken from inlet 2 \;   and velocity 0 is a note off. \; 1 list: note and velocity. \; 1 anything: a message \, see Messages. \; 2 float: velocity for the next note \, 0 to 127 (default 100). \; 3 anything: a message \, the same set as inlet 1. \; 3 float or list: bytes of a SysEx stream \, as sysexin gives \;   them., f 64;
#X obj 60 848 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 876 1 signal: left output. \; 2 signal: right output. \; 3 anything: preset names and state \, as name and value. \; 3 float: SysEx bytes \, see SysEx., f 64;
#X obj 60 954 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 982 preset n: select a patch and report its name. \; presets: report every patch as preset \, number \, name \, \;   then presets and the count. \; info: report the current state \, one message per value. \; bend f: pitch wheel \, -1 to 1 \, times bendrange. \; mod f: modulation lever \, 0 to 1. \; aftertouch f: channel pressure \, 0 to 1. \; sustain 0/1: hold pedal. \; stop: all notes off. \; reset: all notes off and the effect tails emptied., f 64;
#X obj 60 1156 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty MIDI 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1184 notein: note and velocity as a list into inlet 1. \; bendin: scaled to -1..1 and sent as bend. \; ctlin 1: modulation lever \, sent as mod. \; ctlin 64: hold pedal \, sent as sustain. \; touchin: channel pressure \, sent as aftertouch. \; pgmin: program change \, minus 1 \, sent as preset. \; sysexin: straight into inlet 3 \, see SysEx. \; midiout: the floats of the third outlet., f 64;
#X obj 60 1326 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1354 preset (0): patch number \, counted from 0 over all loaded banks. \; volume (80): master volume in percent. \; reverb (patch): reverb balance \, dry to wet. \; chorus (patch): chorus balance \, dry to wet. \; balance (patch): tone balance \, lower tone at 0 \, upper tone at 100. Without effect on patches that use one tone. \; tune (0): master tune in cents. \; voices (8): polyphony per tone. A patch that uses one tone plays twice as many notes. \; bendrange (patch): range of the bend message in semitones., f 64;
#X obj 60 1544 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Data\ files 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1572 The object contains no Roland data. It loads two kinds of file from the folder of the external \, or else from the folder of the patch. \; d50_pcm.bin: the PCM samples \, written by tools/make_d50_data.py from your own ROM images. Without it the object stays silent and says so in the Pd window. \; Every .syx file beside it is read as a D-50 bulk dump of 64 patches. The files are loaded in alphabetical order \, PND50-00.syx first \, and their patches are numbered through. Without a bank the object plays eight built-in presets. \; The engine runs at 32 kHz \, the rate of the original \, and is resampled to the rate of Pd., f 64;
#X obj 60 1778 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Presets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X floatatom 60 1806 4 0 127 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 1830 preset \$1;
#X obj 60 1856 s \$0-d50;
#X obj 190 1806 r \$0-d50-out;
#X obj 190 1830 route preset;
#X obj 190 1856 unpack f s;
#X floatatom 190 1884 4 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X symbolatom 250 1884 22 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X text 82 1912 The patches live in the object. Send preset n to select one. The third outlet answers with the number and the name \, which is all a panel or a headless host needs. \; A patch change resets reverb \, chorus \, equalizer \, balance \, bendrange and portamento to the values stored in the patch., f 64;
#X obj 60 2006 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Patch\ editing 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2034 A message that starts with a section edits the patch that is playing \, at once and without a gap in chorus and reverb. The sections are u1 and u2 for the upper partials \, upper for the upper tone \, l1 \, l2 and lower likewise \, and patch. \; Values are the ones the D-50 shows \, fine for example runs from -50 to 50. Without a value the message reports the current one at the third outlet. All names are listed at the end of this patch. \; An edit lasts until the next preset message unless store was sent. This needs a loaded bank \, the built-in presets cannot be edited., f 64;
#X obj 460 2238 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 2214 6 0 100 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 2238 u1 cutoff \$1;
#X floatatom 160 2214 6 0 30 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 2238 u1 reso \$1;
#X floatatom 260 2214 6 0 100 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 260 2238 u1 level \$1;
#X floatatom 360 2214 6 1 100 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 360 2238 u1 pcm \$1;
#X text 82 2268 u1 cutoff (patch): filter cutoff of the first upper partial. Only synth partials have a filter \, a PCM partial ignores it. \; u1 reso (patch): filter resonance. \; u1 level (patch): level of the partial. \; u1 pcm (patch): PCM sample \, used when the structure makes the partial a PCM one., f 64;
#X obj 460 2392 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 2368 6 1 7 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 2392 upper structure \$1;
#X text 82 2422 upper structure (patch): which partials are synth or PCM and whether they are ring modulated \, see Tone parameters., f 64;
#X obj 460 2482 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 2458 6 0 8 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 2482 patch keymode \$1;
#X text 82 2512 patch keymode (patch): whole \, dual \, split and their solo variants \, see Patch parameters., f 64;
#X obj 60 2558 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Patch\ memory 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 2586 s \$0-d50;
#X msg 60 2586 dump;
#X msg 190 2586 u1 cutoff;
#X msg 320 2586 store;
#X msg 60 2620 param 13 60;
#X msg 190 2620 param 13;
#X msg 320 2620 sysexdump;
#X text 82 2654 u1 cutoff: a section and a name without a value report the value. \; dump: reports the three names and every named parameter \, 311 messages. A panel uses it to show the patch. \; store n: copies the playing patch to slot n \, or to its own slot without n. In memory only \, no .syx file is written. \; param a v: sets one of the 448 bytes of the patch by address \, with the value a D-50 dump stores. The address is the section times 64 plus the offset \, sections counted from 0 in the order u1 \, u2 \, upper \, l1 \, l2 \, lower \, patch. param a reports the byte. \; name: patch name My Patch sets the patch name \, up to 18 characters. upper name and lower name take up to 10. \; sysexdump: sends the playing patch as SysEx \, see below., f 64;
#X obj 60 2876 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty SysEx 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2904 The object speaks the exclusive format of the D-50 \, so an editor or librarian made for the D-50 can program it. Connect sysexin to the third inlet and send the floats of the third outlet to midiout \, as the objects at the top of this patch do. \; Data set (DT1) to address 00-00-00 edits the playing patch \, the same 448 bytes that param reaches. Data set to 02-00-00 replaces patches of the bank of 64 the playing patch is in \, in memory. \; A request (RQ1) for either area is answered at the third outlet. sysexdump sends the playing patch without being asked. \; sysex followed by the bytes of one message does the same from a list. The device number is not checked \, answers carry the number of the request., f 64;
#X obj 60 3126 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Performance 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 3178 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 3154 6 -1 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 3178 bend \$1;
#X floatatom 160 3154 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 3178 mod \$1;
#X floatatom 260 3154 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 260 3178 aftertouch \$1;
#X floatatom 360 3154 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 360 3178 sustain \$1;
#X text 82 3208 bend (0): pitch wheel \, -1 to 1. The range in semitones is bendrange. \; mod (0): modulation lever \, 0 to 1. What it does is part of the patch. \; aftertouch (0): channel pressure \, 0 to 1. \; sustain (0): hold pedal. Notes released while it is 1 sound until it returns to 0., f 64;
#X obj 460 3348 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 3324 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 3348 porta \$1;
#X floatatom 160 3324 6 0 100 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 3348 portatime \$1;
#X text 82 3378 porta (patch): portamento switch. \; portatime (patch): portamento time \, 0 to 100., f 64;
